{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life","id":1043465,"title":"Choosing Supernatural Powers and Merits for YOUR life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T04:32:53-08:00","id":1043465,"title":"Choosing Supernatural Powers and Merits for YOUR life","content":"As you might have guessed by now, I like hypothetical stuff.<br /> One thing that I often thought when reading a WoD or CofD books was: &quot;How cool would that be, if I could do that?&quot;<br /> <br /> So. assuming you could pick any supernatural merits and powers, which ones would you go for and why?<br /> You'd have 9 + (Your age-18) xp to spend. Xp costs are considered in-Clan, in-Family etc. at all times. Your power stat is always 1, your fuel stat is at (your highest resistance trait) and refuels through sleeping. Alternatively, your Willpower can be spend. (You might want to make a char-sheet of yourself for this =D)<br /> <br /> Sole exemption of the rule: Because everyone would pick them for the sheer versitility they offer, you are limited to up to 2 dots of Arcana =P<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd go with Mind 2, the Atavisms Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter, Mimir's Wisdom and the Embed On the Mend.<br /> As I age and get additional xp, I'd get Sleepless, Weatherproof and Acidic Stomach for merits.<br /> Why? Because I feel this combination would make life a lot easier both at work and at some of my hobbies, as well as be sort of something you can rely on in case of emergencies.<br /> So, what about you guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T05:41:43-08:00","id":1043494,"title":"","content":"If my wife was a Sleepwalker, I'd get Time 2 just for Veil of Moments. The only effect you can't get rid of is inability to expend experiences, and while never being able to grow as a person <i>fucking sucks</i> it's trade we'd both make, at least for a little while, to gain functional agelessness. The best part is the ability to turn it off at any time.<br /> <br /> If she wasn't, I'd get Fate 2.<br /> <br /> With Arcana out of the way...<br /> Alien Allure, Mimir's Wisdom, and Wings of the Raptor. Like most human beings, I enjoy being liked, I don't enjoy being lied to, and I think flying would be pretty fucking cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:48:58-08:00","id":1043548,"title":"","content":"Can we pick any template abilities that don't cost experiences cause Mage Sight and Werewolf forms are two powers that jump out at me as some of the first things I would want, but they don't quite fit the exercise as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:23:59-08:00","id":1043564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1043548#post1043548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we pick any template abilities that don't cost experiences cause Mage Sight and Werewolf forms are two powers that jump out at me as some of the first things I would want, but they don't quite fit the exercise as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are out of bounds, as are things like Demon's Eidetic memory /Mulitlingualism/ perfect lying. Or Promethean's Bestowements, Changeling's Blessings, Beast's Skeleton Key and free occult dot etc. Mainly, because I have no idea how to incorporate those into the exercise, and because I think they (Birthrights, Blessings, etc) are simply too different from each other and too tied up to their respective templates in and of themselves.<br /> Sorry =(<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:29:06-08:00","id":1043569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1043564#post1043564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are out of bounds, as are things like Demon's Eidetic memory /Mulitlingualism/ perfect lying. Or Promethean's Bestowements, Changeling's Blessings, Beast's Skeleton Key and free occult dot etc. Mainly, because I have no idea how to incorporate those into the exercise, and because I think they (Birthrights, Blessings, etc) are simply too different from each other and too tied up to their respective templates in and of themselves.<br /> Sorry =(</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, just checking cause if I can't grab Mage Sight or Werewolf Shifting I'll definitely need to snag Auspex and Protean. I'll be back with a character sheet in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:10:41-08:00","id":1043590,"title":"","content":"well, considering that not choosing any Arcana when the option is on the table kinda feels like a waste, I think I'll go with Fate 1. I'll also take Castigation 3, which would be focused for Hellfire, Infernal Visions and Mandate of Hell, and Setto 2. To this I'm adding the In My Pocket Embed and Majesty for 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Fate is to give me a measure of control over the world, but not enough to make me feel as if I'm cheating. Majesty to help me feel liked and in control without actually forcing people to do things against their will (a.k.a Dominate), and it would also help me with using Setto, which would give me a measure of versatility (and besides, I do enjoy trickery). In My Pockets is simply the most useful thing I can think about, so I'm always prepared. Infernal Visions was chosen for the same reason, and Mandate of Hell is an ability which could help dealing with spiritual beings, which as we all know could be problematic at best. Oh, and Hellfire- because I believe I am going to need the firepower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:33:06-08:00","id":1043602,"title":"","content":"The vampire abilities seem pretty tempting, they're good at doing what needs to be done. Dominate has direct applications of mind control as opposed to all the extraneous stuff you wouldn't need with the mind Arcana. It's cheaper, too. But Mind is less confined.<br /> <br /> Question about things like Cruac. Normally when you get a dot of Cruac, you get an associated ritual with it. Would I need dots of Cruac to use these rituals? Or would I just get the rituals, at cost, on their own and use them that way?<br /> <br /> Also you didn't really get into Renown but that tends to be the power stat of most werewolf abilities, I'd assume it's 1, as well? Could it be raised, as Renown had similarities with Cruac, each dot giving you a free Gift Facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:13:16-08:00","id":1043624,"title":"","content":"Just the rituals, without the Cruac is what I'd say right now. Same with Gifts: Assume the requirements for getting anything are gone, except for things that build upon each other (e.g. you cannot have Dominate 4 without Dominate 3) and any supernatural power stat that might figure into the roll is set at 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:21:00-08:00","id":1043627,"title":"","content":"Okay, one last thing, related to Gifts. Shadow Gifts come in groups of five facets, but not sequentually. 'Opening' the Gift takes 3 Experience and gives you a facet, but buying another facet of the Gift costs 2 Experiences. Would you suggest an entire Gift, all five facets, costs 3+2+2+2+2? And just getting 1 would cost 3? Or 2, being effectively 'in Gift.'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T10:40:55-08:00","id":1043631,"title":"","content":"Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 2<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Animalism 1<br /> Cunning 1 (Skin Thief)<br /> Honor 1 (Luna's Embrace)<br /> Mind 2<br /> <br /> Academics 2<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Politics 1<br /> Science 1<br /> <br /> Brawl 1<br /> Drive 1<br /> Survival 1<br /> Weaponry 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 1<br /> Empathy (Reading Emotions) 3<br /> Expression (Acting) 3<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 1<br /> Subterfuge (Hiding Emotions) 2<br /> <br /> Interdisciplinary Specialty (Acting) 1<br /> Resources 1<br /> Sympathetic 2<br /> Tell (Second Skin) 3<br /> <br /> So, I realized it would be more exp efficient to take Second Skin and Skin Thief instead of Protean since the third dot was the only one I cared about, and a fox form is the most important. Not sure if it's cheating to take Tell with my free Merit dots though. Also went with Mind 2 instead of Auspex since Mind can do pretty much all the same stuff and more and I wouldn't have enough experience to get Auspex and another Arcanum. Luna's Embrace was a must-have.<br /> <br /> I would trade all of the above for Time 3, but that's what I'd go for given the two dots in Arcana and no freebie template ability constraints.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, seeing that Renown is free, that might change things. That frees up 4 Experiences, so I might get some Auspex and Fate instead of Mind. Depending on how you want to rule Wolf Gifts and Tells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-04-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:11:50-08:00","id":1043643,"title":"","content":"Query, why is a fox form the most important?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:44:49-08:00","id":1043657,"title":"","content":"@ Gifts: I think it would be more in tune with the rest of the exercise to consider all gifts &quot;open&quot;, thus making buying a whole gift 5 x 2 xp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:52:55-08:00","id":1043661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1043643#post1043643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query, why is a fox form the most important?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my favorite animal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify, I meant that it's the most important animal form for me to have not that having a fox form is the most important supernatural power for me to have. That would go to time travel, but since it requires Time 3, the next highest priority power to me would be Luna's Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-04-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:07:04-08:00","id":1043668,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> So I went over vampire first, but ended up switching to Beast because some of their abilities are basically '1-3 of vampire Disciplines, cheaper.' And because I'm a family man, Life is pretty indispensible, but I would hardly be true to myself if I didn't pick some werewolf Gifts.<br /> <br /> I had a lot of points to deal with, in the end this is what I got.<br /> <br /> Life 3, for 12 Experiences. Oops, had to cut that down to Life 2. The remaining Experiences will go into Hunt of Fire and Ice and Cloak of Mist and Haze.<br /> <br /> From Beast I'd take From the Shadows, Mimir's Wisdom, and Basilisk's Touch, for 9 Experiences.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this only leaves me room for three Gifts. Command Artifice and All Doors Locked are necessities, then I'd go with Unmake for my last 2 Experiences. Because you never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-05-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:54:06-08:00","id":1043713,"title":"","content":"Is it cheating to make Mystery Cults and load them with supernatural merits? I would assume so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:24:37-08:00","id":1043834,"title":"","content":"OK, avoiding Arcana (since they're too <i>easy</i>):<br /> <br /> Mind Control \u2022\u2022\u2022, Telepathy \u2022\u2022\u2022, Biokinesis \u2022, Sleepless \u2022...<br /> <br /> I have 3 xp left over. If I'm allowed to pick homebrew merits, I want all three dots of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/804953-minor-template-the-titov-family\">The Titov Family Magic</a>. But otherwise, I can't think of anything that'd be particularly <i>nice</i> to have for a quiet guy like me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:28:20-08:00","id":1043853,"title":"","content":"Yeah, taking Life dots, or a mix of just about any set of Arcana, would be too obvious for me.<br /> <br /> So, I'd take Half Moon's Gift 5 for 10 XP, Heart of Water, Command Artifice for 4. Calcify the Command, Verto, and Beacon of Helios Alembics for 6. And since I need something for 3, I'll go with Eye of Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:46:31-08:00","id":1043858,"title":"","content":"Tying the Knots of Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Master Shaper \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Phantom Glory \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 both affinities, Control Element metal \u2022\u2022\u2022 both affinities, Discreet conjuration \u2022\u2022\u2022, and Flickering Hours with Fairest Affinity. <br /> <br /> I can warp someones fate, shape the hedge into sentient forms, enter twilight and move through things, become an element, summon an elemental of gold, conjure stuff from my pocket, move faster through the hedge while making myself younger. I'll do a vampire version tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T02:20:42-08:00","id":1043895,"title":"","content":"Some very unexpected things coming around here =D I like!<br /> Loving the Promethean stuff, btw.<br /> <br /> Quick reminder: 2 dots of Arcana at max! So either two 1-Dot Arcana or one at 2 Dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T12:30:34-08:00","id":1044139,"title":"","content":"Interesting hypothetical, let me see. 20xp to work with so probably:<ul><li><b>Arcana: </b>Time 1, Mind 1</li> <li><b>Contracts: </b>Changelin Hours \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Rewind &amp; Freeze, Fairest Variant), Vainglory \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Envoy's Protection &amp; Memories Never Lived, Fairest Variant), Skinmask \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Fairest Variant)</li> <li><b>Embeds: </b>Shift Consequences</li> <li><b>Merits</b>: Brownie's Boon</li> </ul>I'd also go for Pledges and Talecrafting in a heartbeat, but alas those don't have associated exp costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-05-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:27:17-08:00","id":1044183,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I expected Shift Consequences to show up a lot more. So useful, albeit kind of evil.<br /> Brownie's Boon wasn't even on my Radar. For mundane everyday stuff, that's awesome. And those eat up so much time, after all... Interesting choices, PenDragon!<br /> I don't think I've seen anyone settle on a Discipline yet. How curious.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:34:14-08:00","id":1044185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1044183#post1044183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I expected Shift Consequences to show up a lot more. So useful, albeit kind of evil.<br /> Brownie's Boon wasn't even on my Radar. For mundane everyday stuff, that's awesome. And those eat up so much time, after all... Interesting choices, PenDragon!<br /> I don't think I've seen anyone settle on a Discipline yet. How curious.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*rise his hand* well, I took Majesty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:38:58-08:00","id":1044189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1044183#post1044183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I expected Shift Consequences to show up a lot more. So useful, albeit kind of evil.<br /> Brownie's Boon wasn't even on my Radar. For mundane everyday stuff, that's awesome. And those eat up so much time, after all... Interesting choices, PenDragon!<br /> I don't think I've seen anyone settle on a Discipline yet. How curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shift Consequences needn't be super evil. You can easily transfer damage and disaster to things like brick walls and trees, which while still kinda dickish sure beats to hell being shot. I'd forgotten Brownie's boon as well until I went diving through Changeling 2e material. Super useful in real life.<br /> <br /> As disciplines go the only one I'd really go for would be Majesty. However, many of the things disciplines can do can be done slightly cheaper by another splat. Vainglory, for example, covers most of what I'd want out of Majesty and Dominate in a neat, 3xp package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:09:07-08:00","id":1044207,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> Right, sorry! Because you felt it was nicer to the people than Dominate, right?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> You can do that with Shift Consequences? Gosh, I must be a bad person, because the only things I came up with were REALLY mean. Good to know, though.<br /> <br /> Huh. Sounds like Disciplines need a Buff =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:51:50-08:00","id":1044238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1044207#post1044207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Sounds like Disciplines need a Buff =D</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem, as I see it, is the investment and later games, which tend to build off of previously-made games. Requiem set a standard, many of the games since seemed to have worked off of that. For instance the idea of Majesty, though not the specific effects, can be emulated by Beast's cheaper alternative, Alien Allure. Obfuscate 1 and 3 could be replicated by From the Shadows, Auspex by Mimir's Wisdom. Plus we're working off a limited experience pool and Disciplines have to be bought sequentially while many other games offer alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:05:16-08:00","id":1044247,"title":"","content":"I don't like Vampire, so I didn't even look to see if there was anything I'd want. I also made a personal decision not to look at Changeling because the 2e book isn't out and I'm deliberately not burning brain cycles on the game until I have the advance pdf.<br /> <br /> I also don't own Demon, so couldn't pull from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:29:07-08:00","id":1044262,"title":"","content":"I think Disciplines are fine, they're just structured in such a way that if you want, for example, the ability to turn invisible, you can't get that ability as a Discipline without also paying for the ability to become preternaturally unassuming and the ability to make objects similarly unassuming. Which works in Vampire because the different levels of a Discipline represent gradually increasing mastery of a single, powerful supernatural ability. But when the thought experiment is to pick your favorite a-la-carte powers from any splat, people will often want just the invisibility, and often another splat will have that by itself for cheaper. Like with me taking Second Skin and Skinthief instead of Protean 3. Technically, Protean gets me a <i>lot</i> more for the investment - 5xp total to basically be able to turn into a fox whenever I want (or to look like someone I've skinned for a month but I wouldn't ever do that), compared to 9xp to be able to meld into the ground, gain my choice of up to three animal features that I can swap out from day to day, and the ability to turn into up to three different animals whenever I want. But since turning into a fox was the only part I specifically wanted, it those extra abilities weren't worth the extra 4xp, even though they would be for most vampire characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T16:47:16-08:00","id":1044274,"title":"","content":"That too. Something like melding into the earth seems pointless if you're a human who can turn invisible, but if you're a vampire who turns into fire in the sun and sleeps all day it's a huge advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T23:04:32-08:00","id":1044398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1043465-choosing-supernatural-powers-and-merits-for-your-life?p=1044183#post1044183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I expected Shift Consequences to show up a lot more. So useful, albeit kind of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I lived the life of a normal tabletop character it would be in the top spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T04:55:57-08:00","id":1044442,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> that is a very good point. Haven't considered that.<br /> Btw, I think Obfuscate 2 is incredibly more useful in daily life than simply turning invisible =D Melding with the earth would only make sense if you were some sort of survivalist, I guess, then it would be incredibly useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:22:10-08:00","id":1044596,"title":"","content":"A personal selection (because why not go for immortality?) would be: Flickering Hours (Fairest) 4xp, and Hollow (Route Zero) 1xp. I presume it's necessary to buy the 'alternate seeming' thing for an extra xp, and Hollow gives me access to the Hedge so I can actually employ the contract. Spend one point of 'nameless energy' and one WP for activation cost and regain the latter from the Route Zero trip. Easy peasy and as a plus I can spend another point of X fuel to bring my SO along for the ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3139-rayn-faustus","name":"Rayn Faustus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3139_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T09:53:54-08:00","id":1046822,"title":"","content":"That's 19 xp, huh.<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Academics 1<br /> Crafts 1<br /> Computer 2<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Science 3<br /> <br /> Athletics 1<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 1<br /> Weaponry 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 2<br /> Empathy 1<br /> Intimidation 2<br /> Persuasion 2<br /> <br /> Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science)<br /> Language 2<br /> Multilingual 1<br /> Resources 1<br /> Safe Place 1<br /> Retainer 2 - pet dog (2 xp)<br /> <br /> Arcana: Matter 2 (8xp)<br /> Disciplines: Animalism 1 (3 xp)<br /> Contracts: Cloak of the Bear's Massive Form (Beast) (wolf, bat, falcon, mud shark) (4 xp)<br /> Alembics: Mechanicus (Electrification) (2 xp)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:29:23-08:00","id":1046904,"title":"","content":"You probably don't have to pay for a pet dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T02:40:02-08:00","id":1047136,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a>, Yep, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's right. Unless your pet dog is some sort of Temple Guardian Foo Dog like Mouse, your dog would be not included in the xp expenditure - that is for supernatural powers/merits. So 2 more xp, maybe another Alembic?^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-11-2017, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}